title Still in your own half
intro Red has pushed everyone forward.
flip vertical

setup
  lineup 7v7
  player R-CB at 34, 34
  player R-RB at 36, 18
  player R-LB at 36, 52
  player R-CM at 26, 40
  player R-RF at 28, 10
  player R-LF at 28, 60
  player B-CM at 18, 26
  player B-LF at 50, 30
  player B-RF at 28, 50
  ball with B-CM

step
  caption Watch where Blue is when the ball is played. The yellow line is the halfway line.
  draw halfway-line

step
  caption Blue kicks it forward. Their teammate is past every Red outfield player.
  ball to 48, 30
  arrow from B-CM to ball
  draw halfway-line
  duration 1300

question
  prompt Is the Blue striker offside?
  answer No
  wrong Yes
  wrong Yes, they are past everyone
  wrong Only if they score
  correct Not offside.
  why Blue is still on their own side of the halfway line, and you can never be offside in your own half.

question
  prompt What makes it okay?
  answer Blue is in their own half
  wrong Blue ran fast
  wrong The pass was short
  wrong Red was not looking
  correct Blue is in their own half.
  why Offside only counts in the other team's half. Cross that halfway line and the rule switches on.
